In a file window, type a line then erase by word (^W) and line (^U), exercising
ctlw/ctlu and the local-cut backspacing across word boundaries.

-- input --
move 150 4
button 4
move 150 116
button 0
move 100 75
button 4
move 240 165
button 0
move 125 85
button 1
button 0
type aa bb cc
key ctrl-w
key ctrl-w
key ctrl-u
key ctrl-u
key ctrl-w
type dd
key enter
type e
key ctrl-u
key ctrl-u
delay 100
move 50 5
button 1
button 0
-- waitframes --
29 29 51 54 55 55 57 63 107 107 109 109 115 123 132 141 150 159 168 177 187 197 207 207 207 214 222 228 234 241 251 251 251 267 267
